---
layout: base.njk
hideAtmosphere: true
---
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/home.css?v={{ assetv }}">

{% from "icons.njk" import icon %}

{% set liveTools = [] %}
{% for tool in tools %}{% if tool.status == "live" %}{% set liveTools = (liveTools.push(tool), liveTools) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}

<div class="fx-progress" id="fxProgress" aria-hidden="true"></div>

{# Header sits outside .fx-body: that element clips overflow-x, which silently
   kills position:sticky for anything inside it. Inside the frame the homepage
   nav both scrolled away and sat ~inset from where every other page puts it. #}
{% include "header.njk" %}

<div class="fx-body">
<div class="fx-frame">

  <section class="fx-hero" id="fxHero">
    <div class="fx-hero-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="fx-hero-eclipse" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="fx-hero-inner">
      <p class="fx-kicker reveal">One-person software studio</p>
      <h1 class="reveal"><span class="fx-line">Developer and security tools</span><span class="fx-line"><span class="fx-accent">with visible boundaries.</span></span></h1>
      <p class="fx-hero-sub reveal">Penumbra Forge is a one-person studio. I maintain a catalog of mostly small browser-delivered utilities and a few larger software projects. Many work locally; each page labels whether its active route stays in the browser, uses an edge worker, contacts a third party, or sends input to a selected AI endpoint. Most projects are early.</p>
      <div class="fx-hero-actions reveal">
        <a href="/tools/" class="fx-btn fx-btn--solid"><span>Browse small utilities</span></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/penumbraforge" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="fx-btn"><span>Source on GitHub</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="fx-ticker" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="fx-ticker-track">
      {%- for tool in liveTools -%}<a href="/tools/{{ tool.slug }}/" tabindex="-1">{{ tool.name }}</a>{%- endfor -%}
    </div>
    <div class="fx-ticker-track">
      {%- for tool in liveTools -%}<a href="/tools/{{ tool.slug }}/" tabindex="-1">{{ tool.name }}</a>{%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="fx-section-head reveal">
    <span class="fx-index">01</span>
    <h2>Larger projects</h2>
    <span class="fx-rule"></span>
    <span class="fx-count">{{ products | length }} current projects</span>
  </div>

  <div class="fx-bento">
    <div class="fx-cell fx-cell--gate reveal">
      <div class="fx-cell-meta"><span>Secret-pattern scanning</span><span class="fx-status fx-status--dev">experimental</span></div>
      <h3>Gate</h3>
      <p>An experimental local CLI that looks for secret-like patterns in source files and git history. It can install a repository-local pre-commit hook and attempt bounded source rewrites. Pattern matching can produce false positives and misses.</p>
      <div class="fx-term">
        <div class="fx-term-bar">illustrative — gate scan --staged</div>
        <pre><span class="hl-dim">$</span> <span class="hl-key">gate scan --staged</span>

<span class="hl-warn">&#x2718;</span> <span class="hl-str">config/db.yml</span><span class="hl-dim">:12</span>  credential-shaped value
  <span class="hl-dim">matched value redacted from terminal output</span>

<span class="hl-str">1 pattern finding</span> <span class="hl-dim">— inspect the staged diff</span></pre>
      </div>
      <a href="/gate/" class="fx-cell-link">Explore Gate <span>&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>

    <div class="fx-cell fx-cell--librarian reveal">
      <div class="fx-cell-meta"><span>MCP skills server</span><span class="fx-status fx-status--dev">experimental</span></div>
      <h3>mcp-librarian</h3>
      <p>A local Markdown skill library for MCP-speaking clients. BM25 search stays local; web research and pack operations are network tools. Ed25519 status is recorded during indexing, but load responses do not enforce it.</p>
      <div class="fx-featlist"><span>opt-in auto-research</span><span>indexed integrity status</span><span>no external runtime packages</span><span>persistent skills</span></div>
      <a href="/librarian/" class="fx-cell-link">Explore Librarian <span>&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>

    <div class="fx-cell fx-cell--vexes reveal">
      <div class="fx-cell-meta"><span>Dependency scanning</span><span class="fx-status fx-status--dev">experimental</span></div>
      <h3>vexes</h3>
      <p>Matches dependencies against OSV across {{ versions.vexes.ecosystems }} ecosystems and, for npm/PyPI, flags selected code and registry evidence worth reviewing. Heuristics are not verdicts. Still experimental and unproven against real-world attacks.</p>
      <div class="fx-featlist"><span>bounded analysis</span><span>explicit npm guard</span><span>{{ versions.vexes.ecosystems }} ecosystems</span><span>zero external runtime npm deps</span></div>
      <a href="/vexes/" class="fx-cell-link">Explore vexes <span>&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>

    <div class="fx-cell fx-cell--umbra reveal">
      <span class="fx-ghost" aria-hidden="true">{{ icon("crescent", 96) }}</span>
      <div class="fx-cell-meta"><span>Local AI prototype</span><span class="fx-status fx-status--dev">private prototype</span></div>
      <h3>Umbra</h3>
      <p>A private, unreleased local AI application being developed on Apple Silicon with MLX. A working prototype exists, but there is no public build or supported release yet.</p>
      <div class="fx-featlist"><span>Apple Silicon</span><span>MLX</span><span>desktop interface</span><span>no public release</span></div>
      <a href="/umbra/" class="fx-cell-link">Explore Umbra <span>&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="fx-section-head reveal">
    <span class="fx-index">02</span>
    <h2>Local AI</h2>
    <span class="fx-rule"></span>
    <span class="fx-count">two public routes + one private prototype</span>
  </div>

  <div class="fx-principles">
    <div class="fx-principle reveal">
      <span class="fx-glyph">{{ icon("crescent") }}</span>
      <h3>In your browser</h3>
      <p>The five model-backed site tools can use a small quantized model in the browser over WebGPU. Model files download from their host; prompts stay in the tab in this mode. Small models, so expect modest quality.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fx-principle reveal">
      <span class="fx-glyph">{{ icon("home") }}</span>
      <h3>On your machine</h3>
      <p>Those model-backed tools can point at Ollama, LM Studio, or another OpenAI-compatible endpoint on localhost. If you enter a remote endpoint instead, that operator receives the model input.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fx-principle reveal">
      <span class="fx-glyph">{{ icon("chip") }}</span>
      <h3>In the Umbra prototype</h3>
      <p>Umbra's private development build runs local models through Apple MLX on an Apple Silicon Mac. There is no public build or supported hardware matrix yet.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="fx-section-head reveal">
    <span class="fx-index">03</span>
    <h2>Tools</h2>
    <span class="fx-rule"></span>
    <span class="fx-count">{{ liveTools.length }} mostly small utilities</span>
  </div>

  <div class="fx-tools-grid">
    <a href="/tools/passkey-inspector/" class="fx-tool fx-tool--new reveal"><h4>Passkey Inspector</h4><p>Decode WebAuthn attestation &amp; COSE keys.</p><span class="fx-runtime">browser</span></a>
    <a href="/tools/entropy-xray/" class="fx-tool fx-tool--new reveal"><h4>Entropy X-ray</h4><p>Look at byte entropy to spot packed or encrypted data.</p><span class="fx-runtime">browser</span></a>
    <a href="/tools/key-converter/" class="fx-tool fx-tool--new reveal"><h4>Key Converter</h4><p>JWK ↔ PEM, generate keypairs locally.</p><span class="fx-runtime">browser</span></a>
    <a href="/tools/jwt-attack/" class="fx-tool reveal"><h4>JWT Attack Workbench</h4><p>Try common JWT attack classes against a token.</p><span class="fx-runtime">browser</span></a>
    <a href="/tools/site-score/" class="fx-tool reveal"><h4>Site Score</h4><p>Check a URL for common security headers.</p><span class="fx-runtime fx-runtime--edge">edge worker</span></a>
    <a href="/tools/env-analyzer/" class="fx-tool reveal"><h4>.env Exposure Analyzer</h4><p>See what a leaked .env file would expose.</p><span class="fx-runtime">browser</span></a>
    <a href="/tools/redos-tester/" class="fx-tool reveal"><h4>ReDoS Tester</h4><p>Check a regex for catastrophic backtracking.</p><span class="fx-runtime">browser</span></a>
    <a href="/tools/ioc-workbench/" class="fx-tool reveal"><h4>IOC Workbench</h4><p>Extract &amp; defang indicators from reports.</p><span class="fx-runtime">browser</span></a>
  </div>
  <a href="/tools/" class="fx-tools-cta reveal">View all {{ liveTools.length }} utilities &rarr;</a>

  <div class="fx-section-head reveal">
    <span class="fx-index">04</span>
    <h2>How these are built</h2>
    <span class="fx-rule"></span>
    <span class="fx-count">the short version</span>
  </div>

  <div class="fx-principles">
    <div class="fx-principle reveal">
      <span class="fx-glyph">{{ icon("shield") }}</span>
      <h3>Client-side by default</h3>
      <p>Most tools do their work in the page. A few need the network to do their job — those are labelled, so you know before you paste anything in.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fx-principle reveal">
      <span class="fx-glyph">{{ icon("terminal") }}</span>
      <h3>Dependencies are attack surface</h3>
      <p>Mostly built on platform APIs — Web Crypto, Workers, Node built-ins — with few or no third-party packages. Fewer moving parts to trust or keep patched.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fx-principle reveal">
      <span class="fx-glyph">{{ icon("search") }}</span>
      <h3>Visible source, explicit licenses</h3>
      <p>The website source is public to inspect but uses a source-visible, all-rights-reserved license. Gate, vexes, and mcp-librarian publish their own open-source licenses. No accounts; analytics are limited to aggregate traffic measurement.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
</div>

{% include "command-palette.njk" %}

<script>
/* ---- Scroll progress ---- */
(function () {
  var bar = document.getElementById('fxProgress');
  if (!bar) return;
  var ticking = false;
  function upd() {
    var h = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - innerHeight;
    var p = h > 0 ? Math.min(1, scrollY / h) : 0;
    bar.style.setProperty('--p', p.toFixed(4));
    ticking = false;
  }
  addEventListener('scroll', function () { if (!ticking) { requestAnimationFrame(upd); ticking = true; } }, { passive: true });
  upd();
})();

/* ---- Bento cursor glow ---- */
(function () {
  if (matchMedia('(hover: none)').matches) return;
  document.querySelectorAll('.fx-cell').forEach(function (cell) {
    cell.addEventListener('pointermove', function (e) {
      var r = cell.getBoundingClientRect();
      cell.style.setProperty('--mx', (e.clientX - r.left) + 'px');
      cell.style.setProperty('--my', (e.clientY - r.top) + 'px');
    });
  });
})();

</script>
